cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Unsupervised Learning Lab: a notebook-first study of applied unsupervised learning"
abstract: >-
  A notebook-first laboratory for applied unsupervised learning: seventeen
  executed Jupyter notebooks covering segmentation, dimensionality reduction,
  anomaly detection, topic modelling, recommender embeddings, stability
  analysis, consensus and streaming clustering, nonparametric mixtures,
  time-series and graph methods, and deep clustering. They are backed by
  unsup_lab, a typed and tested Python package with deterministic synthetic
  data generators, label-free evaluation and stability tooling, and a
  production layer of CLI, model artifacts and a scoring API.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
# A single identifier: CFF reads a list of licenses as OR, which would wrongly
# imply either license covers the whole work. The code is MIT; the notebooks
# and documentation are CC BY 4.0. See LICENSE and LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt.
license: MIT
